      "message": "onConfirm callback is silently ignored by ConfirmModal — reboot is never triggered.\n\n\nConfirmModal.enqueue() reads req.resolve to wire OK/Cancel:\n\n```\n// ConfirmModal.vue — next()\nthis.resolver \u003d req.resolve || null;\n\n// onOk()\nif (this.resolver) this.resolver(true);  // only fires when resolver is set\n```\n\n\nThe PR emits onConfirm: () \u003d\u003e doReboot(), which is not a property the modal reads. req.resolve is undefined, so resolver is null. When the user clicks Confirm, doReboot() is never called. The dialog closes silently with no reboot. This is a functional regression — the BMC cannot be reboote\n\nRecommendation:\nMatch the $confirm implementation in main.js:161 exactly — wrap the emit in a Promise and pass resolve.\n\n```\nfunction onClick() {\n  new Promise\u003cboolean\u003e((resolve) \u003d\u003e {\n    eventBus.$emit(\u0027confirm:open\u0027, {\n      message: i18n.global.t(\u0027pageRebootBmc.modal.confirmMessage\u0027),\n      title: i18n.global.t(\u0027pageRebootBmc.modal.confirmTitle\u0027),\n      okTitle: i18n.global.t(\u0027global.action.confirm\u0027),\n      cancelTitle: i18n.global.t(\u0027global.action.cancel\u0027),\n      autoFocusButton: \u0027ok\u0027,\n      resolve,\n    });\n  }).then((confirmed) \u003d\u003e {\n    if (confirmed) doReboot();\n  });\n}\n```",
